  "reviewed_source_inventory_digest": "sha256:83c629aa22fba433bbd69e480aa0ecbd0abfdda74dc7dfec2a88758932920577",
  "body": "## Why\n\nCloud initialization and task access need a single Dactyl transport lifecycle with private, durable session custody and honest account readiness.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Route managed discovery, authentication, account completion and native data access through Dactyl.\n- Keep origin/repository/project-bound credentials and pending one-time state in machine-private locked storage; preserve interrupted outcomes without replay.\n- Require server-confirmed completion and an authenticated read before reporting readiness, with explicit pending, denied, action-required and restart-required states.\n- Preserve local independence, feature boundaries, existing source-CI proof and registry release policy; update operator documentation and actual-binary fixture regressions.\n\n## Proof boundary\n\nNative publication is permitted only after full exact-candidate validation against accepted master. Candidate: {{HEAD_SHA}}. Accepted target: {{BASE_SHA}}. Client source initially depends on the Dactyl #100 API, which requires its corresponding published registry artifact before this source can pass the unchanged dependency contract. No source-overlay, hosted PostgreSQL, managed Auth, production entitlement or release result is implied by local fixtures.\n\nCloses #1628.\n",
